role       = "OPERATOR-LOCKED (2026-08-08) bridge doctrine + the reach-vault design ledger: the vessel holds FOREIGN credentials in confidence so a human posts to Bluesky/Kowloon/elsewhere FROM their wiki — Lararium as force-multiplier. The load-bearing split: a foreign credential buys REACH, never IDENTITY, so custody of one never touches the sovereign plane. Four locks — BRIDGE (never present-as-actor, never cap-translation) · OUTWARD-ONLY · MAILBOX-not-seat · DID-method-compatible first. The reach chain TRUNCATES at CONTRACT (a world-readable credential stops being one) and never federates. Names the honeypot hazard and the far-side revocation asymmetry. DESIGN RULINGS: COMPOSE-AND-REQUEST (the glass drafts, the hearth posts — a browser holds no credential) · the vault reads as a cap-tiered BAG so the truncation falls out of a FLOOR the keystone already meets against · a per-service MANIFEST declares edit/thread/length/media/expiry · content-addressed EMIT RECEIPTS carrying the emitting vessel · health-per-credential, never a retry loop. OPEN: OAuth refresh makes the vault non-passive (research+testing owed) · the persona-binding privacy tension at high account cardinality · the CONTRACT floor oracle · credential onboarding · Kowloon actor-key custody."
